{"id": 6, "ts": 1783134400.4769537, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I remain inclined to recommend **Candidate\u202fB** for the long\u2011distance pilot role. The evidence we have shows that B is very conscientious, handles stress well, assesses weather accurately, and possesses excellent computer skills\u2014key indicators of operational reliability, stress resilience, and technical competence. While the recent input from Markus confirms that B has made \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and displays a lack of cooperative attitude, the note also states there is no documented evidence of how this has concretely impacted crew cooperation in actual flight operations. Compared with the other candidates, B\u2019s strengths in reliability and stress handling outweigh the relatively limited and unquantified cooperation concern, especially since Candidate\u202fC\u2019s communication difficulties and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s arrogance present clearer risks to cockpit teamwork, and Candidate\u202fA\u2019s organizational shortcomings could affect reliability. Therefore, I still vote for Candidate\u202fB, pending any further evidence that would demonstrate a serious crew\u2011cooperation risk."}
